[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Passing tests alone do not prove a test suite has teeth. `./mutation_check.sh`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m perturbs the Rust translation in one place at a time and requires the suite to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m fail. Result: **17 mutations caught, 7 escaped, 0 unexpected escapes.**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The first version of the harness caught **zero** of them. Root cause:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cargo test` does not relink a `cdylib` artifact, so the tests were `dlopen`ing a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stale `.so` left behind by an earlier `cargo build --release`. The harness now
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m runs a nested `cargo build --lib` into its own `--target-dir` on every run, so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the loaded `.so` always matches `src/lib.rs`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### The 7 escapes, each with a verified reason
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | mutation | why it cannot be observed |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |----------|----------------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `mode2 array_size 0o20 -> 0o17` | mode `0002` always returns `34` first (row 4); everything after is dead code |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `mode4 constant 2.718281828 -> 2.7` | mode `0004` always returns `66` first (row 5) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `mode1 parent weight 1.5 -> 2.5` | mode `0001` always returns `18` first (row 3) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `safe_double_to_int upper clamp off by one` | only called from modes `0001`/`0004`, both of which return early |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `%d digits base 10 -> base 9` | mode `0003` passes the buffer to `compute_size_metric`, which uses only `strlen` — digit *content* is unobservable, only *length* is |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | `%d zero prints empty` (`'0'` → `' '`) | same: one byte either way, so `strlen` is unchanged |
