[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The two "content is unobservable" rows are not a coverage gap: three separate
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m mutations that change the formatted **length** by ±1 (`%d emits an EXTRA digit`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `%d zero emits NO digit`, `sprintf literal _Depth_ LENGTHENED`) are all caught,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m which proves the length is genuinely under test. Likewise
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `NODE_COUNT starts at 7` — the mutation that simulates
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `initialize_test_data()` actually running — is caught, which is the positive
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m evidence that the dead-code claims above are real and not an excuse.
